            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, this behavior is intentional. It is the result of the combination of the following goals:\r\n- Keep any window's current line (i.e. \"current file system entry\") aligned with what is shown on the right. Otherwise it feels a bit confusing. This is responsible for right part of the currently navigated branch to get trimmed if cursor is moved from its position.\r\n- Fit as much data on the screen as possible. This results into windows shifting to the right if right part of the branch is trimmed.\r\n \r\nThere are several solutions (from most to least robust):\r\n\r\n- Use [\"go out plus\" action](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L157) (which is `H` by default)  instead of just \"go out\" (which is `h` by default). This will trim the right part of the branch after each \"go out\" action. You can switch default keys similar to how [it is shown for \"go in\" action](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L659-L663).\r\n- Manually trim the right part of the branch when needed. Use [\"trim right\" action](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L173) (`>` by default).\r\n- Set `config.windows.preview = true`. This will always show a preview on the right which will allow to navigate (only) one step back without windows getting rearranged.\r\n\r\nHope this helps.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this behavior is intentional. It is the result of the combination of the following goals:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Keep any window's current line (i.e. \"current file system entry\") aligned with what is shown on the right. Otherwise it feels a bit confusing. This is responsible for right part of the currently navigated branch to get trimmed if cursor is moved from its position.</li>\n<li>Fit as much data on the screen as possible. This results into windows shifting to the right if right part of the branch is trimmed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There are several solutions (from most to least robust):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Use <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L157\">\"go out plus\" action</a> (which is <code class=\"notranslate\">H</code> by default)  instead of just \"go out\" (which is <code class=\"notranslate\">h</code> by default). This will trim the right part of the branch after each \"go out\" action. You can switch default keys similar to how <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L659-L663\">it is shown for \"go in\" action</a>.</li>\n<li>Manually trim the right part of the branch when needed. Use <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-files.txt#L173\">\"trim right\" action</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">&gt;</code> by default).</li>\n<li>Set <code class=\"notranslate\">config.windows.preview = true</code>. This will always show a preview on the right which will allow to navigate (only) one step back without windows getting rearranged.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hope this helps.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, this behavior is intentional. It is the result of the combination of the following goals:\n\nKeep any window's current line (i.e. \"current file system entry\") aligned with what is shown on the right. Otherwise it feels a bit confusing. This is responsible for right part of the currently navigated branch to get trimmed if cursor is moved from its position.\nFit as much data on the screen as possible. This results into windows shifting to the right if right part of the branch is trimmed.\n\nThere are several solutions (from most to least robust):\n\nUse \"go out plus\" action (which is H by default)  instead of just \"go out\" (which is h by default). This will trim the right part of the branch after each \"go out\" action. You can switch default keys similar to how it is shown for \"go in\" action.\nManually trim the right part of the branch when needed. Use \"trim right\" action (> by default).\nSet config.windows.preview = true. This will always show a preview on the right which will allow to navigate (only) one step back without windows getting rearranged.\n\nHope this helps.",
