                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with `j`/`k`, especially since we can manually trim it with `>`. But it can only become a problem when we try to perform operations on both the parent and the current directory at the same time (e.g., moving a file).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with <code class=\"notranslate\">j</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">k</code>, especially since we can manually trim it with <code class=\"notranslate\">&gt;</code>. But it can only become a problem when we try to perform operations on both the parent and the current directory at the same time (e.g., moving a file).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with j/k, especially since we can manually trim it with >. But it can only become a problem when we try to perform operations on both the parent and the current directory at the same time (e.g., moving a file).",
