                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with `j`/`k` ...\r\n\r\nIt makes complete sense with `window.preview = true`, which in turn makes it more strange to not follow the logic with `window.preview = false`. But the main driver here is that I do think that it is confusing to allow \"misaligned cursors\": when cursor points to one file system entry, but to the right there is still information about another.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with <code class=\"notranslate\">j</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">k</code> ...</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It makes complete sense with <code class=\"notranslate\">window.preview = true</code>, which in turn makes it more strange to not follow the logic with <code class=\"notranslate\">window.preview = false</code>. But the main driver here is that I do think that it is confusing to allow \"misaligned cursors\": when cursor points to one file system entry, but to the right there is still information about another.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I still think it's strange to automatically trim the tree with j/k ...\n\nIt makes complete sense with window.preview = true, which in turn makes it more strange to not follow the logic with window.preview = false. But the main driver here is that I do think that it is confusing to allow \"misaligned cursors\": when cursor points to one file system entry, but to the right there is still information about another.",
